# Copy to .env for local development. Vite INLINES VITE_* at BUILD time, so a
# build without this value ships a front end that cannot reach the Worker.
# Measured consequence of forgetting it: 7 panels fell from real data to
# "未能讀取數據 — 需要 Worker 代理" and coverage dropped 13/16 to 8/16.
#
# Local development — `cd worker && npx wrangler dev` listens on 8787:
VITE_WORKER_BASE=http://localhost:8787
#
# Production — the deployed Worker, verified live 2026-09-23:
#   https://hk-city-monitor.cyrus738.workers.dev
# Health check: curl <base>/health  →  {"ok":true,"whitelistHosts":67}
# VITE_WORKER_BASE=https://hk-city-monitor.cyrus738.workers.dev
#
# NOTE: this value is embedded in the shipped bundle, which is fine — it is a
# public CORS proxy whose whitelist is enforced server-side. Nothing secret is
# configured here, and the Worker holds no keys.

# Where the LIVE copies of data/aircraft.json, data/berth_vacancy.json and
# data/water_suspension.json are read from — the branch scripts/live_cycle.sh publishes to.
#
# A FORK MUST SET THIS. The built-in default names this project's branch, and reading
# someone else's live data does not announce itself: the payload is well-formed, the
# timestamps are real, it is simply not your data. Format:
#   VITE_LIVE_BASE=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<you>/<repo>/<branch>
# Leave it unset to use the committed snapshots only (panels then age to amber, which is
# honest rather than wrong).
# VITE_LIVE_BASE=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Cyruschu430/hk-city-monitor/live-data
